## CFG-6 · Shipped profiles (the growth ladder)

| profile | chapters | words/ch | max_revisions | prior_summary | max_cost_usd | purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `tiny` | 3 | 300–550 (400) | 2 | 120 | 2 | prove the loop; every demo and test |
| `small` | 6 | 700–1100 (900) | 3 | 200 | 8 | first real story arc |
| `medium` | 12 | 1500–2500 (2000) | 3 | 250 | 25 | novella |
| `full` | 24 | 2500–4000 (3200) | 3 | 300 | 80 | full novel |

Moving up a rung is a one-word change (`"profile": "small"`). **No Python file changes between rungs** — test `CFG-T7` runs the whole pipeline under `mock` for all four profiles and asserts identical code path, only different limits.

---

## CFG-7 · Change specs (how the harness improves incrementally)

Every improvement is a small file in `specs/changes/CHG-NNN-<slug>.md` using this template:

```
# CHG-014 · Raise continuity threshold for medium+ profiles
Motivation: at 12 chapters, drift in character voice slips through at threshold 8.
Change: config only — profiles/medium.json and full.json set quality_gate.threshold = 9.
Code touched: none.
Spec touched: CFG-6 table.
Verification: run tiny (unchanged) and medium under mock; medium shows ≥1 extra rewrite in logs; tiny identical to previous run (same config_hash → same output).
Rollback: revert the two profile files.
```

Rules: one concern per change; `Code touched: none` is the goal and the default; a change that needs code must say which spec ID it amends. `tools/check_specs.py` fails if a `CHG` file lacks any of the six headings.

---

## CFG-8 · Migration

When `schema_version` bumps, ship `tools/migrate_config.py vN → vN+1` that rewrites old files, and add a row to `specs/changes/`. Old snapshots stay readable by the version that wrote them (resume never migrates).

